." Manpage for hsh (Simple Shell)
.TH HSH 1 "26 Aug 2026" "1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a custom UNIX command line interpreter that reads and executes user commands from standard input or file streams. It handles command path resolution, argument parsing, process creation, and standard environment interaction.
.SH INVOCATION
If started without arguments with STDIN attached to a terminal, 
.B hsh
runs in interactive mode and displays the prompt
.I "($) ".
If input is piped, it operates non-interactively and exits after processing standard input. Empty lines or whitespace-only inputs are ignored.
.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell immediately with the status code of the last executed command.
.TP
.B env
Prints all current environment variables inherited from the parent process.
.SH COMMAND EXECUTION
Commands and their arguments are tokenized using spaces and tabs ('\t'). Execution steps:
.IP 1. 3
If the command begins with a slash ('/') or dot ('.'), it is treated as a path and executed directly.
.IP 2. 3
Otherwise, 
.B hsh
searches for the executable across directories listed in the 
.B PATH
environment variable.
.IP 3. 3
Execution creates a child process via
.BR fork (2),
executes via
.BR execve (2)
passing the current environment, and waits for completion using
.BR wait (2).
.SH ERRORS AND EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success or the status code of the executed child process. If a command is not found, 
.B hsh
prints an error formatted as:
.I "<prog_name>: 1: <command>: not found"
to standard error and returns status 127.
